{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Rich previews for files a chat reply points at (a file reference, a link, or a paragraph that is only a path), shared by the desktop (crates/ui/src/markdown/file_preview.rs) and iOS. Paths are cleaned and resolved exactly as local paths in image-sources-v1.json (`file://` (optionally `localhost`) and `cypher-file:` stripped, `?query` and `#fragment` dropped, percent-escapes decoded, a trailing `:12`, `:12-20` or `:12:5` line suffix dropped); URLs and other schemes (`https:`, `data:`, `mailto:`) are never previewed here. `caps` (bytes, rows, characters): `tableReadBytes` = only this much of the head of a csv/tsv file is read; `tableRows` = data rows shown; `columnChars` = the most characters a shown cell has; `pdfMaxBytes`, `videoMaxBytes`, `htmlMaxBytes` (html and svg) = larger files show a 'too large' placeholder instead of a preview. `kinds`: `kind(path)` by the cleaned path's extension, any case: `csv` (.csv), `tsv` (.tsv, .tab), `pdf` (.pdf), `video` (.mp4, .mov, .m4v, .webm), `html` (.html, .htm), `svg` (.svg), else `none` (also a name that is only an extension, like `.csv`). `table`: `parseTable(text, delimiter, complete)` where `text` is what was read (UTF-8, invalid bytes replaced), `delimiter` is `,` (csv) or a tab (tsv) and `complete` is false when `text` is only the head of the file. Rules, in order: (1) one leading U+FEFF is dropped. (2) Records end at CRLF, LF or a lone CR outside quotes; fields split at the delimiter outside quotes. A field whose first character is `\"` is quoted: `\"\"` inside is one `\"`, delimiters and line breaks inside are kept, and characters after the closing quote are appended as written; a `\"` elsewhere is literal. In a complete text an unclosed quote runs to the end. Both delimiters use the same rules. (3) When `complete` is false the last record is dropped unless the text ends with a line break outside quotes (it may be cut). (4) Records that are one empty field (blank lines) are dropped. (5) Each cell shows as: every CRLF, CR or LF replaced by one space, then trimmed of whitespace. (6) The first record is a header when at least one record follows it and its cells are all non-empty, none is numeric, and no two are equal. Numeric: an optional + or -, digits with an optional fraction (or a fraction alone, `.5`), an optional exponent (`e`/`E`, optional sign, digits), an optional trailing `%`; thousands separators are not numeric. (7) `totalRows` = data records (the header excluded); `rows` = the first `tableRows` of them; `columns` = the header's cells (absent when `header` is false). Every shown row and `columns` is padded with empty cells to the widest of them. (8) A cell longer than `columnChars` Unicode scalar values (Swift: `unicodeScalars`, not `count`) keeps its first `columnChars - 1` and ends with `…` (U+2026). (9) `truncated` = not `complete`: the count is then shown as `totalRows`+ (\"20+ rows\"), else exactly. `lines`: `line` is a whole reply paragraph's Markdown source; `src` is the file it shows as a preview block, or null: the paragraph is one token by the image-sources-v1.json `lines` rules (bare, in backticks or in <…>; no whitespace; bare tokens without * [ ] ( ) < > ` !) whose `kind` is not `none`; an svg is null here because it is an image (image-sources-v1.json shows it).",
  "caps": {
    "tableReadBytes": 262144,
    "tableRows": 20,
    "columnChars": 40,
    "pdfMaxBytes": 52428800,
    "videoMaxBytes": 209715200,
    "htmlMaxBytes": 5242880
  },
